# Build context hygiene.
#
# Without this file the Dockerfiles' `COPY . .` pulls whatever happens to sit in
# the checkout into the image — including a local .env. That bakes live secrets
# (DEEPSEEK_API_KEY, SESSION_SECRET, database credentials) into the image layers,
# where they survive in every layer that copied them and travel with the image
# anywhere it is pushed, tagged or exported.
#
# docker compose passes these at runtime instead, via `env_file: .env` and the
# per-service `environment:` blocks, so the running containers still receive them.

# Local configuration and secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
auth.json

# Version control and editor state
.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore
.idea
.vscode
.fleet

# Installed dependencies and build output: each image installs its own, and a
# host copy is the wrong platform anyway.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
public/build
public/hot
public/storage

# Runtime noise and caches
*.log
coverage
.phpunit.cache
.phpunit.result.cache
**/.turbo
**/.cache
